"Infinitely many sign-changing solutions for logarithmic Schrödinger equations via an \\(L^p\\)-perturbation approach (https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.14444)\nciteturn2academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; We study the logarithmic Schrödinger equation \\[ -Δu+V(x)u=u\\log u^2,\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb R^N,\\ N\\ge3. ... We introduce an \\(L^p\\)-regularization perturbation, which restores a \\(C^1\\) variational structure while preserving the logarithmic nonlinearity, and prove via a limiting argument that the original equation admits infinitely many sign-changing weak solutions.\nTitle: Infinitely many sign-changing solutions for logarithmic Schrödinger equations via an \\(L^p\\)-perturbation approach\nAuthors: Chen Huang, Zhipeng Yang, Jiazheng Zhou\nDate: Fri Jun 12 13:24:46 2026\n\nWe study the logarithmic Schrödinger equation \\[ -Δu+V(x)u=u\\log u^2,\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb R^N,\\ N\\ge3. \\] Since the logarithmic energy is not \\(C^1\\) on the natural space \\(H_V^1(\\mathbb R^N)\\), direct invariant-set minimax arguments for sign-changing solutions are not available. We introduce an \\(L^p\\)-regularization perturbation, which restores a \\(C^1\\) variational structure while preserving the logarithmic nonlinearity, and prove via a limiting argument that the original equation admits infinitely many sign-changing weak solutions.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNormalized solutions for logarithmic Schrödinger equation with a perturbation of power law nonlinearity (https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.08237)\nciteturn2academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.5 years ago; Title: Normalized solutions for logarithmic Schrödinger equation with a perturbation of power law nonlinearity ... We study the existence of normalized solutions to the following logarithmic Schr\\\"{o}dinger equation \\begin{equation*}\\label{eqs01} -\\Delta u+\\lambda u=\\alpha u\\log u^2+\\mu|u|^{p-2}u, \\ \\ x\\in\\R^N, \\end{equation*} under the mass constraint \\[ \\int_{\\R^N}u^2\\mathrm{d}x=c^2, \\] where $\\alpha,\\mu\\in \\R$, $N\\ge 2$, $p>2$, $c>0$ is a constant, and $\\lambda\\!\nTitle: Normalized solutions for logarithmic Schrödinger equation with a perturbation of power law nonlinearity\nAuthors: Wei Shuai, Xiaolong Yang\nDate: Mon Apr 17 12:59:03 2023\n\nWe study the existence of normalized solutions to the following logarithmic Schr\\\"{o}dinger equation \\begin{equation*}\\label{eqs01} -\\Delta u+\\lambda u=\\alpha u\\log u^2+\\mu|u|^{p-2}u, \\ \\ x\\in\\R^N, \\end{equation*} under the mass constraint \\[ \\int_{\\R^N}u^2\\mathrm{d}x=c^2, \\] where $\\alpha,\\mu\\in \\R$, $N\\ge 2$, $p>2$, $c>0$ is a constant, and $\\lambda\\!\\in\\!\\R$ appears as Lagrange multiplier. Under different assumptions on $\\alpha,\\mu,p$ and $c$, we prove the existence of ground state solution and excited state solution. The asymptotic behavior of the ground state solution as $\\mu\\to 0$ is also investigated. Our results including the case $\\alpha<0$ or $\\mu<0$, which is less studied in the literature.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n非齐次非线性薛定谔方程新的爆破准则 (https://xblk.ecnu.edu.cn/CN/10.3969/j.issn.1000-5641.201911029)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.2 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; Abstract: In this paper, the existence of blow-up solutions for the nonhomogeneous nonlinear Schrödinger equation is studied. ... Schrödinger equations with a spatially decaying nonlinearity: Existence and stability of standing waves [J].\n\nImage 中文核心期刊\n中国科技核心期刊\n中国科学引文数据库来源期刊\n美国《化学文摘》(CA)收录\n美国《数学评论》(MR)收录\n\n华东师范大学学报（自然科学版） ›› 2020, Vol. 2020 ›› Issue (4): 64-71.doi: 10.3969/j.issn.1000-5641.201911029\n\n\n### 非齐次非线性薛定谔方程新的爆破准则\n\n李双双   \n\n  1. 西北师范大学 数学与统计学院, 兰州 730070\n\n  * `收稿日期:`2019-06-26 `发布日期:`2020-07-20\n  *   * `作者简介:`李双双, 女, 硕士研究生, 研究方向为偏微分方程. E-mail: 18793114195@163.com\n  * `基金资助:`\n\n国家自然科学基金(11601435)\n\n### A new blow-up criterion for the nonhomogeneous nonlinear Schrödinger equation\n\nLI Shuangshuang   \n\n  1. College of Mathematics and Statistics, Northwest Normal University, Lanzhou 730070, China\n\n  * `Received:`2019-06-26 `Published:`2020-07-20\n  *   *   * RichHTML 241\n\nPDF 271\n\n可视化 0\n\n#### 摘要/Abstract\n\n摘要： 本文研究了非齐次非线性薛定谔方程爆破解的存在性. 首先构造了一类不变集, 然后应用最佳Gagliardo-Nirenberg型不等式以及仔细的分析证明了对任意大的$\\mu$, 存在$u_{0}\\in H^{1}$, 使得$E(u_{0})=\\mu$, 并且以$u_{0}$为初值的解$u(t,x)$在有限时间内爆破, 该结果改进了文献[1]中的结果.\n\n[Input] [Input] [Input]\n\n关键词: 非齐次非线性薛定谔方程, 不变集合, 爆破\n\nAbstract: In this paper, the existence of blow-up solutions for the nonhomogeneous nonlinear Schrödinger equation is studied. First, a class of invariant sets is constructed and then the optimal Gagliardo-Nirenberg type inequality is applied; careful analysis is used to prove that for any large $\\mu$, there exists $u_{0}\\in H^{1}$ so that $E(u_{0})=\\mu$ and the solution $u(t,x)$ with $u_{0}$ as an initial value blows up in finite time. This result supplements the existing content in the literature [1].\n\nKey words: nonhomogeneous nonlinear Schrödinger equation, invariant set, blow-up\n\n#### 引用本文\n\n李双双. 非齐次非线性薛定谔方程新的爆破准则[J]. 华东师范大学学报（自然科学版）, 2020, 2020(4): 64-71.\n\nLI Shuangshuang. A new blow-up criterion for the nonhomogeneous nonlinear Schrödinger equation[J]. Journal of East China Normal University(Natural Science), 2020, 2020(4): 64-71.\n\n\n#### 参考文献\n\n[1] FARAH L G. Global well-posedness and blow-up on the energy space for the inhomogeneous nonlinear Schrödinger equations [J]. J Evol Equ, 2016, 16(1): 193-208. DOI: 10.1007/s00028-015-0298-y.\n[2] LIU C S, TRIPATHI V K. Laser guiding in an axially nonumiform plasma channel [J]. Physics of Plasmas, 1994, 1(9): 3100-3103. DOI: 10.1063/1.870501.\n[3] CHEN J Q, GUO B L. Sharp global existence and blowing up results for inhomogeneous Schrödinger equations [J]. Discrete Cont Dyn-B, 2007, 8(2): 357-367. DOI: 10.3934/dcdsb.2007.8.357.\n[4] HMIDI T, KERAANI S. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNumerical solution of the regularized logarithmic Schrödinger equation on unbounded domains - ScienceDirect (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0168927419300352)\nciteturn2search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.4 years ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; It is difficult to develop numerical methods for the logarithmic Schrödinger equation on unbounded domains, due to the blow up of the logarithmic nonlinearity and the unboundedness of the physical domain. ... ### Incoherent white light solitons in logarithmically saturable noninstantaneous nonlinear media\n\n## Applied Numerical Mathematics\n\nVolume 140, June 2019, Pages 91-103\n\n# Numerical solution of the regularized logarithmic Schrödinger equation on unbounded domains\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1016/j.apnum.2019.01.018Get rights and content\n\n## Abstract\n\nThe numerical solution of the logarithmic Schrödinger equation on unbounded domains is considered in this paper. It is difficult to develop numerical methods for the logarithmic Schrödinger equation on unbounded domains, due to the blow up of the logarithmic nonlinearity and the unboundedness of the physical domain. Thus, a regularized version of the logarithmic Schrödinger equation on unbounded domains with a small regularization parameter is developed. Then, the local artificial boundary conditions for the regularized logarithmic Schrödinger equation are designed by applying the unified approach, which based on the idea of well-known operator splitting method. The regularized logarithmic Schrödinger equation defined on unbounded domains is reduced to an initial boundary value problem on the bounded computational domain, which can be solved by the finite difference method. Due to the blow-up of the logarithmic nonlinearity, these mentioned above numerical methods can not be applied to the LogSE directly. Thus, it is not trivial issue to solve the problem (1)–(2). To overcome the difficulty of logarithmic nonlinearity, Bao et al. [8], [9] presented a regularized finite difference method for the LogSE by introducing a proper regularized logarithmic Schrödinger equation (RLogSE) on bounded domain, and analyzed the error estimates. However, since the fairly expensive for large domain in practical computations, it is cumbersome from a numerical point of view and requires the solution to remain compactly supported for all time. In particular it is not true for large classes of solitary waves like the nonlinear Schrödinger equation. Moreover, the mass of the exact solution for the original problem set on the whole space is conserved whereas the mass of the restricted solution should decrease [28]. Thus, it is important to design the suitable boundary conditions to lead to a well-posed initial boundary value problem.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2021wakate_program (https://www2.kobe-u.ac.jp/~ueda/Wakate42/2021wakate_program.pdf)\nciteturn2search14 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 10 months ago;   Finite time blow-up of solutions to an attraction-repulsion chemotaxis system in higher dimensions ...   ポテンシャル項付き非線形 Schrödinger 方程式の最小質量爆発解 ...   Logarithmically Improved Extension Criteria Involving the Pressure for the Navier-Stokes Equations in R³\n9月1日（水）\n\n第13セッション　座長：檜垣 充朗（神戸大学）\n\n- 9:30–9:55　浜野 大（埼玉大学）  \n  逆霧乗型ポテンシャルをもつ非線形シュレディンガー方程式の球対称散乱解について\n\n- 10:00–10:25　Hughes, David（東北大学）  \n  Large-time behavior of solutions to the surface quasi-geostrophic equation\n\n— 休憩 —\n\n第14セッション　座長：水上 雅昭（京都教育大学）\n\n- 10:40–11:05　藤原 瑠（明治大学）  \n  非局所被食者・捕食者モデルの不連続定常解\n\n- 11:10–11:35　藤井 幹大（九州大学）  \n  水平方向にのみ粘性をもつ3次元異方的 Navier-Stokes 方程式の解の漸近挙動\n\n- 11:40–12:05　細野 竜也（東北大学）  \n  Finite time blow-up of solutions to an attraction-repulsion chemotaxis system in higher dimensions\n\n— 昼食 —\n\n第15セッション　座長：黒田 隆徳（早稲田大学）\n\n- 13:30–13:55　松井 一徳（金沢大学）  \n  Navier-Stokes 方程式に対する全圧境界条件を課した場合の射影法\n\n- 14:00–14:25　松井 直己（東京理科大学）  \n  ポテンシャル項付き非線形 Schrödinger 方程式